              "explanation": "Ingestion endpoints enforce W3C SHACL shape validation (targetClass, required properties, datatype constraints) before mutating graph state.",
              "options": [
                "It bypasses all validation to maximize ingestion speed",
                "Every node must pass through W3C SHACL shape validation gates before being committed",
                "It only allows ingestion of plain markdown files",
                "It requires manual human approval for every individual file"
              ],
              "question": "How does the KGraph Parse Portal guarantee that ingested nodes do not corrupt the Knowledge Graph?"
            },
            {
              "answer": "packages/kgraph-parse-portal/bin/luxir-portal-cli.js",
              "explanation": "luxir-portal-cli.js enables searching, raw JSON document inspection, and daemon health checks directly from the command line.",
              "options": [
                "npm test",
                "kubectl get pods",
                "packages/kgraph-parse-portal/bin/luxir-portal-cli.js",
                "git log"
              ],
              "question": "Which CLI tool provides direct terminal access to search, inspect, and monitor the Luxir engine?"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Module 5: Luxir C++ Hybrid Search Index Bridge & W3C SHACL Validation Gates"
        }
      ],
